codex
Defects found:

- Lines 80 and 323-324: input `outputs/.paper_figures_rollout.lock` already exists with `111@010101`, then run `python scripts/rollout_figures_2026_08_20.py`. The refused second process still enters `finally` and `release_lock()` deletes the first process’s live lock, allowing concurrent rollouts.

- Line 234: input `pr={"topic":"T","slots":1,"drawn":1,"declined":0,"has_outcome":true}` and committed page body `<section id="pn-paper"><h3>Paper</h3><figure>not drawn.</figure></section>`. It marks the page `ALREADY DELIVERED` solely because slot count matches, so wrong drawn/declined content is never rebuilt.

- Lines 252-259 and 317: input ledger with one predicted page, and a `build_tabbed.py` invocation that returns nonzero. The page is recorded in `led["failed"]`, but `main()` still returns `0`, so a wrapper/CI gate sees success while work failed.

- Lines 130-131: input `<section id="pn-paper"><figure><div aria-label="Forest plot"></div></figure></section>`. `observe()` returns `slots=1`, `drawn=1`, `declined=1`, so one figure is counted as both drawn and declined.

- Lines 135 and 275: before input `<section id="pn-paper"><h3>Paper</h3></section>`, after input `<section id="pn-paper"><h3>Paper</h3><figure><h3>Figure title</h3><svg></svg></figure></section>`. A heading inside a figure satisfies the “exactly +1 section” check even though no section was added.

- Lines 61 and 129: input `<section id="pn-paper"><figure class="paper-figure"><svg></svg></figure></section>`. The regex matches only literal `<figure>`, so a valid figure element with attributes is invisible to the slot/drawn/declined guard.

No proven finding from this packet for CRLF/LF text comparison, merged-cell tabulation, or negation-dropped matching.
